# broiler-shared-package pin 1
#
# One package of the committed, hash-pinned feed (decision SJL-D-4 (c); milestone SJL-2.7): a shared
# JavaScript library package whose home is the Broiler.JS repository, retained here byte for byte so
# that a restore needs no other repository's folder and no network for it. NuGet.config's package
# source mapping sends the Broiler.ECMAScript prefix to this directory and to nuget.org; the lock
# file of a project that references it records `content-hash`, and rule I1 holds that hash to this
# pin and to the allow-list.
#
# HOW IT WAS TAKEN. The package exactly as the Broiler.JS repository's publish-shared workflow pushed
# it to nuget.org on 2026-10-13 (run 38376970162, its artifact shared-packages), packed from
# `upstream-commit`; the nuspec's repository element records the same commit, which rule I7 reads.
# nuget.org serves the same package with its repository signature (.signature.p7s) added, and NuGet's
# content hash of a signed package leaves the signature out, so a restore from either source records
# `content-hash`, the base64 SHA-512 of this file's bytes. `sha256` is over the same bytes.
#
# (Revised 2026-10-13, when the package was published. The copy committed on 2026-10-12 was packed
# locally from 93df3fd, whose library sources the published commit holds unchanged; its bytes differ
# from the published package's, so this feed now holds the published package, and a restore from
# either source records one hash. The paragraph read: "Packed on 2026-10-12 in the Broiler.JS
# repository, from `upstream-commit`, with `dotnet pack Broiler.ECMAScript/Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms
# -c Release -p:Version=<version> -p:PackageVersion=<version> -p:ContinuousIntegrationBuild=true`; the
# nuspec's repository element records the same commit, which rule I7 reads. `content-hash` is NuGet's:
# the base64 SHA-512 of the .nupkg's bytes, which is what a lock file records. `sha256` is over the
# same bytes." The identity lines read:
#   content-hash T2OSjZRPalI2gOn70yimlFuzYHxzzD7bXtrN5XfYJtykuBnnunK5OgMEuvoXGKbxgmmO8zQK9RyZbduleSWpBw==
#   sha256 ac24cc4ff5a26668542e24fb278075e44bd74cdbb65b7050957974af39d87c47
#   upstream-commit 93df3fd4d5d469268fbd2324b1f4f9ede0d2110c)
#
# WHAT IT IS. The first preview of the shared algorithms library's number-conversion area (milestone
# SJL-3.3; JSD-0065): admitted for PRODUCT use by Broiler.VM.Profile.JavaScript and
# Broiler.VM.Profile.JavaScript.Compiler at SJL-3.4, and restored by the admission probe. It is on
# nuget.org since 2026-10-13, as a Broiler.VM package release that depends on it requires
# (eng/verify-feed.ps1).

id Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms
version 0.1.0-preview.1
